{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LOOP ITERATION 3 — prep for this ADR while J9's plan review is in flight (deliberately not starting a\nsecond concurrent review: the brainstorm log records that concurrent reviews worsened the Anthropic\nAPI failures, and a --status call once blocked ~10 min on the store lock).\n\nMECHANICAL FACTS for whoever writes the ADR:\n * Next free ADR number is 0055 (highest present is 0054).\n * CAUTION — THREE files already share the number 0035:\n     docs/adr/0035-rc2b-snapshot-horizon-safe-replay.md\n     docs/adr/0035-code-review-two-lane-tier-tagged-impact.md\n     docs/adr/0035-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md\n   This story amends the THIRD one. Any 'see ADR 0035' reference written without the slug is\n   ambiguous in this repo, so cite the filename, not just the number.\n * That file's structure is Context / Decision / lettered subsections — e.g. '(a) Jira-coupling\n   inventory' — so the amendment should follow the same shape rather than inventing one.\n\nSUBSTANCE ALREADY RECORDED on this ticket (see the earlier comment): the port-incompleteness finding\nand the RemoteRef.instance gap. Both are now backed by more evidence than when I wrote that comment:\n\n * The port declares SIX TicketTransport members; the core reaches for TWENTY-ONE. TWELVE are absent\n   from the DC transport, and the same twelve are declared on no Protocol at all. Measured by AST\n   audit over every attribute access on a client/transport receiver.\n * The dominant failure mode is SILENT: 7 of the 12 are swallowed by 'except Exception' at every call\n   site, 3 are mixed, 1 crashes, 1 is hasattr-guarded. So a DC deployment appears to converge while\n   not syncing comments, links, parents, properties, or validating assignees.\n * ROOT CAUSE is now separately ticketed as [rebar:cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8]: the core passes the transport\n   as an UNANNOTATED parameter, so mypy cannot enforce port completeness. Proven three ways —\n   unannotated: no error; 'client: Any': no error; 'client: TicketTransport': mypy rejects the\n   undeclared call. The ADR's claim that 'the contract suite certifies a backend' holds only as far as\n   the port is complete AND typed.\n\nThe ADR should state that conditionality plainly, because epic be74 (GitHub Issues) inherits the same\nseam and will hit the same wall otherwise."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785483845327052001,"uuid":"58dbbbdf-016f-4a9b-b6bb-e9b701f2d7d2"}